                <pb facs="0487" n="1221" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1221"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Interview with the minister for foreign affairs. Presented demand. He said he had
                    no knowledge of the case, but promised to communicate with Cuba at once, in
                    order to answer as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taylor.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
